WEBVTT

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:31.720
<i>The seeds of worries that I thought I got 
rid of burst out my mind and sprouted</i>

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:47.950
<i>Today again, countless brambles 
spread out underfoot, awaiting me</i>

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:56.410
<i>Where do I go in order to meet you?</i>

00:00:56.410 --> 00:01:11.300
<i>Don't hold me, the thorns 
on my back will hurt you</i>

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:26.530
<i>But still, my overflowing 
emotions are searching for you</i>

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:36.030
"The Village of Granites"

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:43.490
Whoa! Look, Clain! It's got some 
snacks and a stuffed animal!

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:45.900
You're carefree, aren't you?

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:48.250
Considering we could get killed...

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:52.240
<i>I guess that's not really the case 
for her since she's a doppel, huh?</i>

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:52.840
<i>Then...</i>

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:55.700
The only one getting killed is me...

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:03.810
Ow...

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:06.270
Oof.

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:11.390
Just how long are you guys 
gonna stay in that net?

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:12.610
Are you tuna or something?

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.440
Tuna?!

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:16.620
Hurry up and get out!

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:28.650
Amazing!

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:31.950
Ah, h-hey, you!

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.000
Ah, Clain! That's not fair!

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:33.000
Geez...!

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:35.000
Hold it!

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:38.840
These are all amazing antiques!

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:42.200
To think that physical 
monitors are still in use!

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:44.560
Yellow flowers are blooming!

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:46.760
What're you doing, acting on your own?!

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:48.190
You're our prisone...

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:50.440
Whoa! That's incredible, too!

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:53.130
Not again...

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:58.320
If you act carelessly, that 
thing will be fired at you.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:04.700
Whoa! To think that he's 
using an optical sight!

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:06.290
Th-This place is heaven!

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:08.620
If you keep it up, I'm really 
gonna send you to heaven!

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:13.670
Hello!

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:15.380
Enri!

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:16.550
Welcome back!

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:19.800
I'm back. Did you finish your homework?

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:20.470
Yep!

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:22.010
Welcome back.

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:24.470
Oh, this is the boy Sunda was looking for?

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:25.630
Yep.

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:31.440
Oh geez...

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:39.080
We've got another guest!

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:43.280
Nice to meet you! Let's shake hands!

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:54.420
Enri, is there a doppel over there?

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:55.540
Yeah.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:01.590
Oh, hello. Those are fashionable 
clothes you're wearing.

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:04.640
Oh yeah. Let me get a closer look at them.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:07.970
Thank you, Enri!

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:08.640
Humph!

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:10.640
What's going on?

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:13.100
Why couldn't they see Nessa at first?

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:13.740
That's because...

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:15.690
Get away from them!

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.650
You'll be corrupted by their bad customs.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:20.610
Corrupted?

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:22.470
Humph!

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:28.080
Okay, greeting time is over. 
Big Brother is waiting.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.010
Hey, you're here!

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:45.550
Welcome... to Granites Village!

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:52.450
Let's have a talk, Boy...

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:54.850
a deep man-to-man talk!

00:04:57.860 --> 00:04:59.000
Huh?!

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:02.030
What do you wanna do?

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:04.320
That man dislikes Nessa.

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:05.030
What?

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:09.160
Those who dislike Nessa can't touch Nessa!

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:10.030
Nessa...

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:12.330
Nessa will stay with Enri.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:13.410
Huh?!

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:17.040
Enri, let's go! Show Nessa your treasure!

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:20.250
H-Hey! What do you mean by my treasure?!

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:21.840
Hurry!

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.960
Wait up!

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.010
Let's see...

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:35.020
So, Boy...

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:36.890
What is it, "Boy"?

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:39.190
The lost millennium...

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:40.610
What?

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:42.650
The thousand years post-Fractale...

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:45.070
Those are the years of depravation.

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:49.620
Humans completely depended on Fractale 
and lost their pride and grit.

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:51.500
Depravation...?

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:57.500
The Lost Millennium rose up in order 
to release people from Fractale.

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:03.710
Even within the Lost Millennium, we, 
Granites, are a relatively big faction.

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:05.710
L-Lost Millenni...

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:09.130
Whoa... so I got captured 
by a terrorist group?

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:10.760
Have some coffee before it gets cold.

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:12.090
Y-Yeah...

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:18.390
This coffee was produced in this village.

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:20.810
What?

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:24.530
We produce everything we eat and drink...

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:26.990
without depending on doppels.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.700
We teach kids using books...

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:34.660
so that they learn to think using their 
own head without depending on data.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:40.290
Everyone here had their 
Fractale Terminals removed.

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:41.460
They removed their terminals?

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:43.320
That's right.

00:06:43.810 --> 00:06:47.510
Fractale took away humans' 
natural way of living!

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:49.550
It took away humans' pride!

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:51.930
Whoa! Where's the dish towel?

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:55.140
Natural life starts with natural drying.

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:56.350
What the heck's that mean?

00:06:56.690 --> 00:06:59.600
The Fractale System is 
now starting to collapse.

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:02.650
The fact that balloons keep falling all 
over the place is the proof of that.

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:07.530
The temple says that the Fractale 
System is God's divine protection,

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:10.990
but they just say that so they 
can control us however they want!

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:13.160
And, it's already collapsed!

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:16.040
I don't quite get what you're saying,

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:19.580
but why was the L.M. after Phryne?

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:22.540
That woman you spent the night with...

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:23.920
No! That's...

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:28.130
is a priestess at the temple and 
will become the key to this world.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.880
Key to the world?

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:35.470
That woman ran away from the temple... 
with a doppel, in other words, with data.

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:37.970
Are you talking about Nessa?

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:39.930
It's a doppel that woman went to the trouble

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:41.390
to take with her when she 
ran off from the temple!

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:43.150
Just as I thought...

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:47.400
There must be important data 
hidden inside that doppel!

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:50.960
Now that we've obtained 
that, our victory is...

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:01.000
Obtained it? But Nessa is...

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.830
You guys are already inside this village.

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:07.320
In other words... you're 
what they call hostages.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:12.010
You sure walk fast, Enri.

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:15.470
Nessa thinks that there's no 
need to be in such a hurry.

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:17.430
Geez... Then don't follow me!

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:23.480
Whoa!

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:25.350
Is this your house, Enri?

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:27.230
No. It's our mother ship.

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:29.940
A ship? So there's treasure in it?

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:34.110
Anyway, go back to that kid!

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:34.880
Humph!

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:42.250
Geez, what's with that 
doppel? It's too friendly!

00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:43.880
Enri!

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:46.790
Seriously...

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:49.550
Your condition check is completed.

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:52.090
Your condition today is...

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:53.880
You had a little too much sugar!

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:57.220
So you wanted to go to the bathroom, huh?

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:59.390
Ah, remember to wipe your butt, okay?

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:00.360
Wha...?!

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:07.730
Hello?! Hello?!

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:12.350
<i>Hostages, huh?</i>

00:09:12.350 --> 00:09:14.680
<i>This is a fine mess I've 
gotten myself into...</i>

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:23.040
I-It hurts!

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:24.660
Calm down. We'll give him a sedative.

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:30.920
Could this place possibly be a hospital?

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:31.500
Yeah.

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:35.420
We do have inpatient facilities, 
too, but we don't have enough beds.

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:37.130
So we handle simple treatments here.

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:42.140
I've never seen so many patients 
gathered like this before.

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:45.480
If you access Fractale, you can 
receive high-level medical service

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:48.650
whenever you like and 
wherever you prefer, so...

00:09:49.010 --> 00:09:50.610
But in this village...

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:53.150
Then you shouldn't have 
removed the terminals.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:56.610
We do that to fight to the end 
as a soldier of Lost Millennium.

00:09:57.450 --> 00:10:01.270
It means that although it's very 
tough for us, we still choose...

00:10:01.270 --> 00:10:03.620
true freedom!

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:04.870
Freedom?

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.540
You don't know true freedom!

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:11.340
My knees are not doing well.

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:14.920
I'm sorry, but please wait a little longer.

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:22.600
Clain!

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:24.470
Do you wanna know the 
color of Enri's underwear?

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:25.770
Ahh! Don't tell him!

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:28.140
<i>True freedom...</i>

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:30.350
I don't really get it.

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:32.310
I don't even wanna know something like that.

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:34.730
Wha... You didn't have to say it that way.

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:38.070
I won't tell you anyway!

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.000
Clain?

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:45.910
Well then, cheers...!

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:50.060
No, before that, put your 
visors on, everyone!

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:56.480
Amazing!

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:57.920
What a sophisticated doppel!

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:00.120
Now, let's toast!

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:01.510
To the Granites' guests!

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:02.680
Cheers!

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:07.470
Cute!

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:16.270
What's wrong, Clain?

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:19.360
I don't know how to deal with people here.

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:20.200
Huh?

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:22.980
They stubbornly believe in nonsensical ideas.

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:25.660
They appear to be nice people, 
but I can't trust them.

00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:30.710
Here.

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:33.080
What's this?

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:35.460
It's a soup made of beans and smellie grass.

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:38.920
What?! Aren't you gonna eat it?!

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:41.090
I-I will.

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:43.460
<i>I'm always eating tubes, so...</i>

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:49.930
This taste is something else!

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:50.430
Huh?

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:52.570
It has a very complicated taste and...

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:56.940
What's this? It's sweet and then it's salty.

00:11:56.940 --> 00:12:00.490
Geez, just say if it's good or bad already!

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:03.160
It's good... very good.

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:05.740
Glad to hear that.

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:06.580
Have more.

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:09.910
What's the matter?

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:13.170
You don't like beans?

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:14.080
It's not that.

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:18.710
Granny, there's no way a doppel 
would have a meal, right?

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:21.510
Oh, that's right. I'm sorry.

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:33.310
They said that you could use this place.

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:35.190
Don't go overboard with the naughty stuff.

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:37.610
Like I said...!

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:42.530
<i>Why is there only one bed?</i>

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:44.900
<i>They keep saying "naughty, naughty."</i>

00:12:44.900 --> 00:12:47.350
<i>Who'd be interested in a kid like Nessa?</i>

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:50.790
Nessa?

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:53.460
What did the soup of beans 
and smellie grass taste like?

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:56.670
What? Well... it tasted good.

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:59.000
It was salty and a little sweet.

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:01.150
Explain in more detail.

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:04.050
The beans were soft.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:06.090
Besides that, let's see...

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:07.800
I might've tasted a little bitterness...

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:10.980
Nessa doesn't understand what you're saying!

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:14.390
Express the taste by dancing!

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:16.600
Huh?! Dance to express the taste?!

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:20.070
Nessa can't eat food, so...

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:21.920
Nessa...

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:25.510
Nessa can't understand unless 
you apply it to something else.

00:13:29.650 --> 00:13:32.910
I-It might be something like this...

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:35.080
You mean the taste is like sneaking around?

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:39.380
No! It's more like this, and it's like "bam!"

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:41.840
That's a very happy exciting taste!

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:43.050
Then, then, what did the 
pancakes taste like?!

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:46.060
Let's see... I-It was like this...

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:49.260
It's like crawling around, huh?

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:53.220
Hey, hey, it's touching this!

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:55.600
They're getting pretty lively, aren't they?

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:58.190
Just as you'd expect from him.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:17.660
What's the matter, Clain?

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:23.880
Say, what's going on? A festival?

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:27.720
We got a report that they suddenly 
decided to hold the Star Festival.

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:28.930
What?

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:31.550
I wonder why the temple is so anxious.

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:32.800
The Star Festival...

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:36.020
That's an event where the priestesses 
at the temple pray to the stars, right?

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:38.070
Butcher, get moving!

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:40.650
The site is three sectors away from here!

00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:42.360
Hurry up or the festival will be over!

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:43.400
Yes, Sir!

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:46.320
What are you going to do?

00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:48.490
Huh? Are you half-asleep?

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:51.200
Of course, we're gonna 
go disrupt the festival!

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:52.020
What?!

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:56.240
You too, put on those clothes!

00:14:56.240 --> 00:14:57.950
M-Me, too?

00:14:57.950 --> 00:15:00.580
Star Festival, huh? Nessa's 
looking forward to it.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:02.940
What're you saying? You're a hostage.

00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:04.250
Of course, you'll stay here!

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:06.130
What?!

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:30.820
<i>Whoa... Everything is antique!</i>

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:35.410
<i>I-I'm so excited!</i>

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:39.000
Listen! Some of us may 
get injured or even die,

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:42.580
but we must stop the Star Festival 
no matter what! Got that?!

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:43.210
Yes, Sir!

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:46.290
Get injured or die? It's just a festival.

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:49.300
You can't see it at all, can you?

00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:51.800
That's because you have the 
terminal inside your body.

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:53.840
You can no longer see the truth.

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:55.050
What a foolish existence...

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:58.770
I bet he got stupid because he 
does too much naughty stuff.

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:02.350
Wh-Why do you have to go so far 
with all this "naughty" stuff?!

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:05.980
That's right! Clain isn't 
really <i>that</i> naughty!

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:11.650
Ah! I thought we left you in the village!

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:14.280
Well, I thought this would happen, though.

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:18.990
She's just data. No matter where 
we confine her, it's no use.

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:21.830
Just data...

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:24.080
I see, that's why the bathroom...

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:24.640
Bathroom?

00:16:24.640 --> 00:16:26.790
I-It's nothing!

00:16:27.270 --> 00:16:28.250
We can see it now.

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:32.300
What is the Star Festival?

00:16:33.170 --> 00:16:35.570
Okay, Boy, try answering that question.

00:16:35.570 --> 00:16:37.180
Come on, I know that much.

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:41.730
On the night of the new moon, 
many stars... balloons, gather.

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:43.640
Priestesses say a prayer to them.

00:16:44.270 --> 00:16:46.150
Unless you participate in the Star Festival,

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:48.110
you can't receive divine 
protection from the stars.

00:16:48.390 --> 00:16:51.900
For example, if you don't go to the 
festival, your doppel starts acting up.

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:56.240
So even people who aren't very religious 
would participate at any cost.

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:57.840
I'd give that answer 70%.

00:16:57.840 --> 00:16:58.320
What?

00:16:58.850 --> 00:17:02.580
Have you ever thought about why you 
can't receive divine protection anymore?

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:08.720
Leader, if we get any closer 
than this, they'll detect us.

